const SIMS=[
{id:'crash',title:`Pods in CrashLoopBackOff`,brief:`Pager at 7:10 pm: the api service is down. kubectl get pods shows api-7d9f in CrashLoopBackOff with 6 restarts.`,steps:[
 {q:`What's your first move?`,opts:[
  {cmd:`kubectl logs api-7d9f --previous`,out:`Traceback (most recent call last):
  File "/app/main.py", line 8, in <module>
    DB = os.environ["DATABASE_URL"]
KeyError: 'DATABASE_URL'`,ok:true,why:`--previous shows the last crashed run. The cause is right there: a missing environment variable.`},
  {cmd:`kubectl delete pod api-7d9f`,out:`pod "api-7d9f" deleted
api-8c2a   0/1   CrashLoopBackOff   3   45s`,ok:false,why:`Deleting just restarts the loop on a new pod. You've learned nothing about the cause.`},
  {cmd:`kubectl scale deploy/api --replicas=10`,out:`deployment.apps/api scaled
10 pods … CrashLoopBackOff`,ok:false,why:`More copies of a crashing app only multiply the noise and the alerts.`}]},
 {q:`The app can't find DATABASE_URL. What changed recently?`,opts:[
  {cmd:`kubectl rollout history deploy/api`,out:`REVISION  CHANGE-CAUSE
12        release v2.3.0
13        v2.3.1: move env vars to ConfigMap api-config`,ok:true,why:`A rollout 20 minutes ago moved config into a ConfigMap — that lines up with the crash.`},
  {cmd:`kubectl get nodes`,out:`NAME     STATUS   AGE
node-1   Ready    41d
node-2   Ready    41d`,ok:false,why:`Nodes are healthy. The failure is inside the container, not the cluster.`},
  {cmd:`kubectl top pods`,out:`api-8c2a   2m   18Mi`,ok:false,why:`It isn't a resource problem — the process exits on start-up.`}]},
 {q:`Revision 13 moved env vars into a ConfigMap. Check it.`,opts:[
  {cmd:`kubectl get configmap api-config -o yaml`,out:`data:
  DB_URL: postgres://orders-db:5432/orders
  LOG_LEVEL: info`,ok:true,why:`Found it: the key is DB_URL, but the app reads DATABASE_URL. A rename slipped through review.`},
  {cmd:`kubectl rollout restart deploy/api`,out:`deployment.apps/api restarted
api-9f1b   0/1   CrashLoopBackOff`,ok:false,why:`Restarting re-reads the same broken config.`},
  {cmd:`kubectl exec -it api-8c2a -- sh`,out:`error: unable to upgrade connection: container not found ("api")`,ok:false,why:`You can't exec into a container that keeps dying. Read config and logs instead.`}]}],
 root:`A ConfigMap key was renamed (DATABASE_URL → DB_URL) in the latest rollout, so the app crashed on start-up.`,
 fix:`Restore service first with kubectl rollout undo deploy/api. Then fix the key, and add a start-up config check plus a CI test that fails when required variables are missing.`},
{id:'disk',title:`Disk full on web01`,brief:`Alert: web01 root filesystem at 100%. The app is returning HTTP 500s.`,steps:[
 {q:`Confirm what's full.`,opts:[
  {cmd:`df -h`,out:`Filesystem  Size  Used Avail Use% Mounted on
/dev/sda1    50G   50G     0 100% /`,ok:true,why:`Root is completely full. Now find what's using it.`},
  {cmd:`free -h`,out:`        total  used  free
Mem:     16Gi   5Gi  11Gi`,ok:false,why:`That's memory, not disk.`},
  {cmd:`sudo reboot`,out:`Connection to web01 closed.
(back in 3 min — still 100% full, and you've had a full outage)`,ok:false,why:`Rebooting doesn't free disk and causes a bigger outage.`}]},
 {q:`Find the biggest directories.`,opts:[
  {cmd:`sudo du -xh /var --max-depth=2 | sort -h | tail -5`,out:`1.2G /var/lib/apt
2.1G /var/cache
37G  /var/log/app
38G  /var/log
41G  /var`,ok:true,why:`/var/log/app holds 37 GB — a runaway log.`},
  {cmd:`sudo rm -rf /var/*`,out:`(you just deleted package databases, spools and app state)`,ok:false,why:`Never delete blindly. Find the culprit first.`},
  {cmd:`ls /`,out:`bin boot dev etc home lib opt proc root sbin srv sys tmp usr var`,ok:false,why:`Doesn't tell you sizes.`}]},
 {q:`You deleted app.log (37 GB), but df still shows 100%. Why?`,opts:[
  {cmd:`sudo lsof +L1`,out:`COMMAND  PID  USER  FD  SIZE/OFF    NLINK NAME
java    2211 app   7w  39728947200    0 /var/log/app/app.log (deleted)`,ok:true,why:`The Java process still has the deleted file open, so the space isn't released until it closes it.`},
  {cmd:`sudo rm /var/log/app/app.log`,out:`rm: cannot remove '/var/log/app/app.log': No such file or directory`,ok:false,why:`It's already gone from the directory — something still holds it open.`},
  {cmd:`df -h`,out:`/dev/sda1  50G  50G  0 100% /`,ok:false,why:`Same answer. You need to find who holds the file.`}]}],
 root:`Debug logging was left on, app.log grew to 37 GB, and deleting it didn't free space because the process kept the file open.`,
 fix:`Restart or signal the process (or truncate with : > file instead of deleting). Set log level back to info, add logrotate with size limits, and alert at 80% disk.`},
{id:'bad502',title:`502s after a deploy`,brief:`Right after release v1.5, users get 502 Bad Gateway from the load balancer.`,steps:[
 {q:`Where do you look first?`,opts:[
  {cmd:`aws elbv2 describe-target-health --target-group-arn $TG`,out:`Target  Port  State      Reason
i-0a1   8080  unhealthy  Target.ResponseCodeMismatch (health check got 404)
i-0b2   8080  unhealthy  Target.ResponseCodeMismatch (health check got 404)`,ok:true,why:`Every target is failing its health check with 404, so the LB has nowhere to send traffic.`},
  {cmd:`curl -I https://shop.example.com`,out:`HTTP/2 502`,ok:false,why:`Confirms the symptom, but tells you nothing new.`},
  {cmd:`dig shop.example.com`,out:`shop.example.com. 60 IN A 13.234.10.20`,ok:false,why:`DNS resolves fine; the request reaches the LB.`}]},
 {q:`The health check gets a 404. Why now?`,opts:[
  {cmd:`git diff v1.4 v1.5 -- app/routes.py`,out:`-@app.get("/health")
+@app.get("/healthz")`,ok:true,why:`v1.5 renamed the health endpoint, but the load balancer still checks /health.`},
  {cmd:`kubectl get svc`,out:`(this service runs on EC2, not Kubernetes)`,ok:false,why:`Wrong platform — check what actually changed in the release.`},
  {cmd:`sudo systemctl restart nginx`,out:`(still 502)`,ok:false,why:`The app is running fine; the LB just thinks it's unhealthy.`}]},
 {q:`What's the best fix right now?`,opts:[
  {cmd:`Roll back to v1.4, then re-ship v1.5 with /health kept as an alias`,out:`Targets healthy in 30s. 502s stop.`,ok:true,why:`Restore service first, then fix forward safely.`},
  {cmd:`Disable the load balancer health checks`,out:`Traffic now goes to instances even when they're broken.`,ok:false,why:`That removes your safety net for every future failure.`},
  {cmd:`Add more instances`,out:`New instances are unhealthy too.`,ok:false,why:`Scaling doesn't fix a wrong health-check path.`}]}],
 root:`Release v1.5 renamed /health to /healthz, so every target failed the load balancer's health check.`,
 fix:`Roll back, keep /health as an alias, and add a contract or smoke test in CI that calls the health path the load balancer uses.`},
{id:'latency',title:`Checkout got slow`,brief:`After the 6 pm release, p99 latency on the checkout API jumped from 300 ms to 2.8 s. Error rate is normal.`,steps:[
 {q:`Narrow it down.`,opts:[
  {cmd:`histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le, route) (rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))`,out:`/checkout     2.81s
/cart         0.21s
/products     0.18s`,ok:true,why:`Only /checkout is slow — so it's specific to that code path, not the whole system.`},
  {cmd:`Restart all pods`,out:`(p99 still 2.8s after restart)`,ok:false,why:`Restarting without a hypothesis wastes time and hides evidence.`},
  {cmd:`Add two more nodes`,out:`(CPU was 30% — latency unchanged)`,ok:false,why:`There's no saturation, so capacity isn't the issue.`}]},
 {q:`Where is /checkout spending its time?`,opts:[
  {cmd:`Open a slow /checkout trace`,out:`checkout.handler          2.79s
  ├─ auth.verify            0.02s
  └─ db.query orders        2.68s  SELECT * FROM orders WHERE user_id = $1`,ok:true,why:`One database query takes almost all of the time.`},
  {cmd:`Check DNS latency`,out:`avg 2ms`,ok:false,why:`Not the bottleneck.`},
  {cmd:`top on an app node`,out:`load 0.6, CPU 28%`,ok:false,why:`The app is waiting, not working.`}]},
 {q:`Why is that query slow now?`,opts:[
  {cmd:`EXPLAIN SELECT * FROM orders WHERE user_id = 42;`,out:`Seq Scan on orders  (cost=0.00..98211.00 rows=4200000)
  Filter: (user_id = 42)`,ok:true,why:`A full table scan of 4.2M rows — the index on user_id is gone. The release's migration dropped it.`},
  {cmd:`Double the database instance size`,out:`(p99 2.1s — still bad, cost doubled)`,ok:false,why:`Throwing hardware at a missing index barely helps.`},
  {cmd:`Add a Redis cache for orders`,out:`(weeks of work; cache misses still slow)`,ok:false,why:`Fix the cause before adding layers.`}]}],
 root:`A migration in the release dropped the index on orders.user_id, turning a lookup into a 4.2M-row scan.`,
 fix:`Recreate the index (CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY to avoid locking), and add a migration review step plus a performance test on key queries in CI.`}];

