const G=(id,u)=>[`Glassdoor · ${id}`,u];
const REP2=[
[`Are you a self-learner? Give an example.`,`Say yes and prove it with something recent and concrete: what you taught yourself, how (docs, labs, a project), and what you can now do. Tie it to the role, e.g. Kubernetes or Terraform you picked up through hands-on labs while working full time.`,G(`HSBC DevOps Engineer`,`https://www.glassdoor.com/Interview/HSBC-Interview-E3482-RVW94598130.htm`)],
[`Write SQL for a few scenarios: second-highest salary, employees per department, departments with no employees.`,`Second highest: SELECT MAX(salary) FROM emp WHERE salary < (SELECT MAX(salary) FROM emp). Per department: SELECT dept_id, COUNT(*) FROM emp GROUP BY dept_id. No employees: SELECT d.* FROM dept d LEFT JOIN emp e ON e.dept_id = d.id WHERE e.id IS NULL. Talk through NULLs, ties (DENSE_RANK) and indexes.`,[`HSBC Software Engineer, Hyderabad · Taro`,`https://www.jointaro.com/interviews/companies/hsbc/experiences/software-engineer-hyderabad-telangana-january-1-2025-no-offer-positive-3dc543a3`]],
[`Implement a queue from scratch.`,`In Python, use collections.deque (O(1) append and popleft), or build it from two stacks: push onto "in"; when "out" is empty move everything across, then pop from "out" — amortised O(1). A plain list with pop(0) is O(n), so say why you avoid it.`,G(`HSBC (Hyderabad)`,`https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Interview/HSBC-Interview-E3482-RVW100417578.htm`)],
[`Walk me through a technical challenge you faced and how you solved it.`,`Pick one with a real diagnosis: symptom → evidence you gathered → hypotheses → how you isolated the cause → fix → what you changed so it doesn't recur. Numbers and a clear owner hand-off make it credible. Your Stories tab has drafts.`,[`HSBC (Hyderabad) · Taro`,`https://www.jointaro.com/interviews/companies/hsbc/experiences/trainee-software-engineer-hyderabad-telangana-november-2-2025-accepted-offer-positive-39b7ed99`]],
[`Explain a Docker multi-stage build and why you'd use one.`,`Build in a full image (compilers, dev dependencies), then COPY --from=build only the artefacts into a small runtime image. Result: much smaller images, fewer packages to patch, no build tools or secrets in production. Example: FROM python:3.12 AS build → pip wheel; FROM python:3.12-slim → install the wheels only.`,G(`Qualcomm Senior DevOps`,`https://www.glassdoor.com.hk/Interview/Qualcomm-Interview-E640-RVW83397024.htm`)],
[`What is a Kubernetes securityContext? What would you set?`,`Pod- or container-level security settings: runAsNonRoot: true, runAsUser, readOnlyRootFilesystem: true, allowPrivilegeEscalation: false, capabilities drop ALL, and a seccompProfile of RuntimeDefault. Enforce them cluster-wide with Pod Security Admission (restricted).`,G(`Qualcomm Senior DevOps`,`https://www.glassdoor.com.hk/Interview/Qualcomm-Interview-E640-RVW83397024.htm`)],
[`grep the IP addresses out of a log file and count them.`,`grep -oE '([0-9]{1,3}\\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}' app.log | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head. In Python: re.findall with the same pattern, then collections.Counter(...).most_common(10). Mention that the regex doesn't validate 0–255 unless you add checks.`,G(`Qualcomm Senior DevOps`,`https://www.glassdoor.com.hk/Interview/Qualcomm-Interview-E640-RVW83397024.htm`)],
[`Python: fetch JSON data and query it. Then rotate a string anticlockwise by k.`,`JSON: data = requests.get(url, timeout=10).json(), then filter with a comprehension, e.g. [u["name"] for u in data if u["active"]]; handle missing keys with .get(). Rotate left by k: k %= len(s); s[k:] + s[:k] (right rotation is s[-k:] + s[:-k]). Guard the empty string.`,[`Qualcomm Senior DevOps · Glassdoor`,`https://fr.glassdoor.be/Entretien/Qualcomm-Entretien-E640-RVW83397024.htm`]],
[`Python deep-dive: exception handling, OOP concepts, nested dictionaries.`,`Exceptions: try/except specific types, else for the success path, finally for cleanup, raise ... from e to keep context, custom exception classes. OOP: encapsulation, inheritance, polymorphism, composition over inheritance, dunder methods. Nested dicts: d.get("a", {}).get("b"), setdefault, defaultdict(dict), and walking them recursively.`,G(`Qualcomm Python Automation`,`https://www.glassdoor.ie/Interview/Qualcomm-Interview-E640-RVW28725634.htm`)],
[`How would you design for high availability, and where do containers and CI/CD fit?`,`Remove single points of failure: multiple instances across zones behind a load balancer, health checks, stateless app tier, replicated data, and automated failover you've tested. Containers make instances identical and quick to replace; CI/CD makes changes small, tested and reversible (canary, quick rollback). Measure it with SLOs.`,[`Microsoft SRE, Hyderabad · Taro`,`https://www.jointaro.com/interviews/companies/microsoft/experiences/site-reliability-engineer-hyderabad-april-1-2019-no-offer-positive-efe21c7b`]],
[`Network protocols and cloud basics: what happens when you open a URL?`,`DNS resolves the name (cache → resolver → authoritative), TCP three-way handshake, TLS handshake (certificate check, key exchange), HTTP request, load balancer → app → database, response, then the browser renders. Know ports (53, 443), TCP vs UDP, and where a CDN and load balancer sit in the cloud.`,G(`Microsoft SRE/DevOps`,`https://www.glassdoor.ie/Interview/Microsoft-Interview-E1651-RVW87027347.htm`)],
[`Design a lightbulb. (Open-ended design question.)`,`The test is whether you ask before designing: who uses it, where (home, factory, outdoors), what matters (cost, efficiency, lifetime, smart control), constraints (power, safety, regulation). Then propose, state trade-offs, and say how you'd measure success. The same habit wins system-design rounds.`,G(`Microsoft (Hyderabad)`,`https://www.glassdoor.com/Interview/Microsoft-Interview-E1651-RVW37116105.htm`)],
[`Difference between UNION and UNION ALL?`,`UNION removes duplicate rows (so it sorts or hashes — slower); UNION ALL keeps every row and is faster. Use UNION ALL unless you need de-duplication. Both need the same number of columns with compatible types.`,G(`Amgen Data Engineer`,`https://www.glassdoor.com/Interview/Amgen-Interview-E1130-RVW49710804.htm`)],
[`What are NumPy and pandas used for?`,`NumPy: fast n-dimensional arrays and vectorised maths. pandas: tables (DataFrames) built on NumPy for loading, cleaning, joining, grouping and summarising data — e.g. read a CSV of test results, groupby test name, and compute failure rates.`,G(`Amgen`,`https://www.glassdoor.com.au/Interview/Amgen-Interview-E1130-RVW98799199.htm`)],
[`What do you know about Amgen, and why do you want to join?`,`Amgen is a large biotech company making medicines for serious illnesses; its Hyderabad technology centre builds platforms, data and automation for the global business. Connect your strengths — reliable automation, validation discipline, data protection — to regulated, high-stakes software where quality matters. Read their latest annual report before the call.`,G(`Amgen`,`https://www.glassdoor.com.au/Interview/Amgen-Interview-E1130-RVW98799199.htm`)],
[`Explain TCP windowing.`,`The receiver advertises a window: how many bytes it can accept before the sender must wait for acknowledgements. It's flow control. Congestion control (slow start, congestion window) separately limits the sender to protect the network. Throughput ≈ window ÷ round-trip time, so long, fast links need window scaling.`,G(`F5`,`https://www.glassdoor.com.au/Interview/F5-Interview-E9222-RVW94708880.htm`)],
[`How does a server send its response back through the load balancer instead of directly to the client?`,`With source NAT (SNAT) the load balancer replaces the client IP with its own, so the server replies to the load balancer, which forwards to the client. Alternatives: make the load balancer the server's default gateway, or Direct Server Return, where the server replies straight to the client. If you SNAT, pass the real client IP in X-Forwarded-For or PROXY protocol.`,G(`F5 Software Engineer II`,`https://www.glassdoor.co.uk/Interview/F5-Interview-E9222-RVW50163821.htm`)],
[`OS fundamentals: process vs thread.`,`A process has its own address space; threads share their process's memory, so they're cheaper to create and switch but need synchronisation. A crash in one thread can take down the process. Know context switches, and that in CPython the GIL limits CPU-bound threads.`,G(`F5 (Hyderabad)`,`https://www.glassdoor.co.uk/Interview/F5-Interview-E9222-RVW64187845.htm`)],
[`What are hooks and dependencies in pytest?`,`Hooks are plugin functions pytest calls at set points — in conftest.py, e.g. pytest_addoption, pytest_collection_modifyitems, pytest_runtest_makereport. "Dependencies" usually means fixtures depending on other fixtures, so pytest builds them in order with scopes. Explicit test-order dependencies need a plugin and are a smell.`,[`CyberArk Sr. SDET, Hyderabad · Taro`,`https://www.jointaro.com/interviews/companies/cyberark/experiences/sr-sdet-hyderabad-telangana-october-1-2025-no-offer-positive-aef41cfd/`]],
[`How would you design a scalable test automation framework?`,`Layers: test cases → domain helpers/page objects → clients (API, SSH, UI) → config and test data → reporting. Add fixtures for setup, parallel execution (pytest-xdist), tagging, retries only for known infrastructure flakiness, environment config by file or env vars, and CI integration with JUnit reports. Keep tests independent so they can run in any order.`,G(`Netomi SDET`,`https://www.glassdoor.co.uk/Interview/Netomi-Interview-E2854590-RVW103005542.htm`)],
[`Which OOP concepts are used in your framework, and how do you run tests in parallel?`,`Encapsulation (clients and page objects hide details), inheritance (a base test or client class), polymorphism (one interface, platform-specific implementations — e.g. Linux vs AIX vs Windows). Parallel: pytest-xdist (-n auto) with tests that share no state, unique test data per worker, and session-scoped resources made thread/worker-safe.`,G(`Wipro SDET`,`https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Interview/Wipro-Interview-E9936-RVW66807590.htm`)],
[`How does your framework implement commonly used methods?`,`Put shared actions in one place: a utilities or client layer (run_command, wait_until, retry, parse_output), fixtures for setup and teardown, and base classes for shared behaviour. Tests call intent-level helpers, so a product change is fixed in one spot.`,G(`Serrala SDET (Pune)`,`https://www.glassdoor.co.uk/Interview/Serrala-Interview-E2137389-RVW99665712.htm`)]];
{let n=CARDS.filter(c=>c.tr==='rep').length;REP2.forEach(([q,a,src])=>CARDS.push({k:'rep'+(n++),tr:'rep',q,a,src}))}

const HR=[
[`Tell me about your current role and why you're looking.`,`One minute: your title and scope, two results with numbers, and a forward-looking reason (scope, ownership, the kind of work). Never criticise your employer.`],
[`What's your notice period? Can you join earlier?`,`State it plainly, then show flexibility: "It's N days; I can ask for an early release or buy out part of it." Only promise what you can deliver.`],
[`What are your current CTC and expected CTC?`,`Give your current CTC accurately if asked (it may be verified). For expected, give a researched range based on the role and market, not a percentage of your current pay, and say you're flexible for the right role. Let them make the first number where you can.`],
[`Do you have other offers or interviews in progress?`,`Be honest and brief: "I'm in process with a couple of companies; this role is my priority because…" It signals demand without bluffing.`],
[`Are you open to relocating, hybrid or office work?`,`Answer directly with your real constraints and preferences. Confirm the location and work model in writing before accepting.`],
[`What would make you accept a counter-offer from your current company?`,`Show you've thought it through: "I'm leaving for scope and growth, not only pay, so a counter-offer wouldn't change the reasons." Then mean it.`],
[`Why should we hire you?`,`Three matches between the job description and your proof (results, not adjectives), plus one thing you'd add that others might not.`],
[`What is your biggest weakness?`,`A real, work-relevant weakness, what you've done about it, and evidence it's improving. Avoid fake ones ("I work too hard").`],
[`When can you start, and is there anything that could delay joining?`,`Give a realistic date from your notice period, mention any planned leave up front, and confirm you'll share documents for background verification promptly.`],
[`How do you compare two offers?`,`Fixed pay first (variable is uncertain), then role scope and team, learning, stability, location and work model, benefits (insurance, PF, leave), and the growth path. Ask for the full CTC breakdown in writing.`],
[`How do you negotiate after an offer?`,`Thank them, express enthusiasm, then ask once with a specific, researched number and your reason (market data, a competing offer, scope). Negotiate the total — joining bonus, fixed vs variable, level — not just base. Get the final offer in writing.`],
[`What questions should you ask HR before accepting?`,`Fixed vs variable split and how the variable is paid; probation and notice terms; level/band; joining bonus and clawback; work model and location; leave and insurance; background-check process and timeline; first-year appraisal cycle.`]];
HR.forEach(([q,a],i)=>CARDS.push({k:'hr'+i,tr:'hr',q,a}));
DECK.hr=`HR & offer`;
{const swap=(tr,arr)=>{if(!arr||!arr.length)return;for(let i=CARDS.length-1;i>=0;i--)if(CARDS[i].tr===tr)CARDS.splice(i,1);arr.forEach(([q,a,src],i)=>CARDS.push({k:tr+i,tr,q,a,src}))};swap('hr',P.hr)}

